./server
```

### Explanation

- The server listens on TCP port 888.
- It accepts one incoming connection.
- It reads data in chunks up to 1023 bytes, printing out received data until the client disconnects.
- It uses blocking calls, so the program will wait on `accept()` and `read()` until data arrives.

